upstream: https://docs.stripe.com/.well-known/skills/stripe-best-practices
index: https://docs.stripe.com/.well-known/skills/index.json
verified: 2026-11-22
scope: directory
reason: official hosted files still emit broken or non-link targets (2026-11-22: 10 `<references/x.md>` autolinks in SKILL.md, one wrong same-document anchor in
  references/connect.md, one dead Treasury API URL in references/treasury.md)
note: every file listed by the index was fetched 2026-09-29 and adopted verbatim,
  except for these link-target rewrites (link text and all prose unchanged):
  1. SKILL.md, 11 links: upstream rewrites the bundled references as
     `https://docs.stripe.com/references/<name>.md`, which returns HTTP 404
     (measured for all six). Local uses the bundled relative path
     `references/<name>.md`.
  2. references/tax.md, 4 links: upstream emits
     `https://docs.stripe.com/undefined.md#<anchor>` (HTTP 404). Each anchor is a
     heading in the same file, so local uses the same-document target
     `#<anchor>` (threshold-and-nexus-monitoring,
     verify-before-you-trust-automatic-tax, diagnose-zero-tax,
     choosing-a-product-tax-code).
note: known upstream 404 NOT patched, because no verified replacement exists:
  references/treasury.md links https://docs.stripe.com/api/v2/core/vault/financial-accounts.md.
note: frontmatter description is upstream's, unedited.
would_lose_if_wired: a byte-for-byte refresh would restore 15 broken link
  targets (11 cross-file 404s in SKILL.md, 4 undefined.md targets in tax.md)
  and fail repository Markdown-link validation.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is
  present, before any fetch or write.
to_vendor: remove this ledger only after the official hosted SKILL.md uses
  relative reference paths and tax.md uses valid same-document anchors, and
  every indexed file is re-verified. No external publication was performed.
recheck: 2026-10-02 — all 7 indexed files re-fetched (index lists no new files). Adopted upstream: API
  version 2026-09-30.endive, tax.md wording, and upstream's own fix of the registration-safety link
  (now plain text). Link rewrites re-applied: 11 in SKILL.md, 4 in tax.md; all still 404 upstream, as
  does the unpatched treasury vault link. github.com/stripe/ai skills/stripe-best-practices lags the
  hosted index (still 2026-08-26.dahlia), so the hosted index remains the source.
recheck: 2026-11-22 — all 7 indexed files re-fetched; the index now lists 11 skills but the stripe-best-practices entry is still
  exactly these 7 files. Adopted upstream verbatim: API version 2026-11-18.endive, SDK table (Node 23.2.0 and the others), the
  `stripe sandbox create` install wording, Accounts v2 existing-v1-platform guidance and Account Links v2, sandbox wording, Stripe Tax
  registration/threshold/tax-behavior sections, risk-side billing webhooks. The three link defects below are re-applied; everything else
  is upstream text. The earlier 11 absolute `https://docs.stripe.com/references/<name>.md` links and 4 `undefined.md#anchor` links are gone
  upstream (measured: 0 of each), so those two rewrites are retired.
  Current rewrites (text unchanged):
  1. SKILL.md, 10 links: upstream wrote `<references/payments.md>` (angle autolinks, which are not Markdown links to a bundled file
     and which skill-check cannot resolve); local writes `[references/payments.md](references/payments.md)`.
  2. references/connect.md, 1 anchor: upstream links `#existing-platforms` but the heading is "Existing v1 platforms" (anchor
     `#existing-v1-platforms`); local uses the real anchor.
  3. references/treasury.md, 1 URL: upstream's `https://docs.stripe.com/api/v2/core/vault/financial-accounts.md` and
     `POST /v2/core/vault/financial_accounts` return HTTP 404; the live v2 Financial Accounts reference is
     `https://docs.stripe.com/api/v2/money-management/financial-accounts.md` (HTTP 200, "The Financial Account object",
     `POST /v2/money_management/financial_accounts`). Local uses it. This retires the earlier "known upstream 404, not patched" note.
  Frontmatter description is still the 2026-10-30 efficiency-pass rewrite (<=250 chars); upstream's is 1,000+ characters. SKILL.md body is
  upstream's, so a refresh must keep the local description and re-apply the three rewrites above.
description: 2026-10-30 skill-efficiency pass — frontmatter description rewritten to ≤250 chars (what + boundary front-loaded; Codex truncates at ~250). Body untouched by this pass. Re-apply after a byte-for-byte refresh; see docs/skill-efficiency-audit-2026-10-30.md.
